{"parentUuid":"995edb07-aede-4896-a7cf-93a326bb5b82","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7db41848a47c8250","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01TqyYNDeXr7akwN3xxwKFKr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QULiYyuPod8PyWCfQTTLa3","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Benders decomposition SDP master problem combinatorial optimization"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8057,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":387,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8057},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":387,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8057,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox22rFhuFXG6tyciv9k","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3492440e-ed24-4460-bf12-872a09f22b5a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:51:59.138Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ed8b789c-5742-4ce6-befa-46494b1e8dc2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a7db41848a47c8250","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TuNjTQ9Dsgv1ZAgdM579DP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"semidefinite programming VLSI placement floorplanning quadratic\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Global Approaches for Facility Layout and VLSI Floorplanning | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-1-4614-0769-0_29\"},{\"title\":\"Global lower bounds for the VLSI macrocell floorplanning problem using semidefinite optimization | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/1530956/\"},{\"title\":\"Global Approaches for Facility Layout and VLSI Floorplanning | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/265195140_Global_Approaches_for_Facility_Layout_and_VLSI_Floorplanning\"},{\"title\":\"VLSI layout – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/category/applications-science-engineering/vlsi-layout/\"},{\"title\":\"A computational study and survey of methods for the single-row facility layout problem | Computational Optimization and Applications | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10589-012-9505-8\"},{\"title\":\"A nonlinear optimization methodology for VLSI fixed-outline floorplanning | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220089287_A_nonlinear_optimization_methodology_for_VLSI_fixed-outline_floorplanning\"},{\"title\":\"Novel Convex Optimization Approaches for VLSI Floorplanning by Chaomin Luo\",\"url\":\"https://collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/thesescanada/vol2/002/NR43308.PDF?is_thesis=1&oclc_number=663713229\"},{\"title\":\"Semidefinite Programming\",\"url\":\"https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/papers/pdf/semidef_prog.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"QPLIB: a library of quadratic programming instances | Mathematical Programming Computation | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12532-018-0147-4\"},{\"title\":\"Semidefinite programming - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semidefinite_programming\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the intersection of semidefinite programming, VLSI placement, floorplanning, and quadratic optimization:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Semidefinite Programming Applications to VLSI Floorplanning:**\n\nSemidefinite programming (SDP) techniques have been investigated for application to the VLSI macrocell floorplanning problem, with researchers proposing mixed-integer SDP formulations that lead to new SDP relaxations.\n\nSemidefinite optimization approaches can provide global optimal solutions for instances with up to 40 facilities, and tight global bounds for instances with up to 100 facilities.\n\n**Quadratic Formulations and Single-Row Facility Layout:**\n\nThe single-row facility layout problem (SRFLP) is an NP-hard combinatorial optimization problem that arranges departments on a line so as to minimize the weighted sum of distances between department pairs. Recent SDP approaches have been applied to SRFLP by using general quadratic ordering problem formulations.\n\n**Broader Context:**\n\nConic optimization approaches have been successfully applied to two classes of problems: the single-row facility layout problem, and fixed-outline floorplanning in VLSI circuit design. All linear programs and convex quadratic programs can be expressed as SDPs, and via hierarchies of SDPs the solutions of polynomial optimization problems can be approximated.\n\nThese research areas demonstrate the effectiveness of combining semidefinite programming with quadratic formulations for optimizing VLSI placement and floorplanning problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"06ffff09-bb56-4428-a7b9-5b636d8f3e21","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:03.652Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ed8b789c-5742-4ce6-befa-46494b1e8dc2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"995edb07-aede-4896-a7cf-93a326bb5b82","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a7db41848a47c8250","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JuRWCrdk6fb2fAqsdrxW9x","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Mosek SDP solver benchmark 2025 problem size limit variables\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MOSEK\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/latest/docs/S_MOSEK.html\"},{\"title\":\"How to improve the numerical stability for a large SDP using MOSEK - CVX Forum: a community-driven support forum\",\"url\":\"https://ask.cvxr.com/t/how-to-improve-the-numerical-stability-for-a-large-sdp-using-mosek/13552\"},{\"title\":\"Maximum number of SDP vars in Mosek SDP solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/mosek/c/51zaxb8tjvU\"},{\"title\":\"MOSEK Modeling Cookbook Release 3.4.0 MOSEK ApS 05 November 2025\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mosek.com/MOSEKModelingCookbook-a4paper.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The optimizers for continuous problems\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mosek.com/7.0/capi/The_optimizers_for_continuous_problems.html\"},{\"title\":\"MOSEK - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MOSEK\"},{\"title\":\"13.4 The Optimizer for Mixed-Integer Problems — MOSEK Fusion API for C++ 11.1.11\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mosek.com/latest/cxxfusion/mip-optimizer.html\"},{\"title\":\"Mosek ApS\",\"url\":\"https://www.mosek.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Which algorithm is most robust and efficient for solving large scale semidefinite programming (SDP) problem.? | ResearchGate\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/post/Which_algorithm_is_most_robust_and_efficient_for_solving_large_scale_semidefinite_programming_SDP_problem\"},{\"title\":\"MOSEK — AMPL Resources\",\"url\":\"https://dev.ampl.com/solvers/mosek/index.html\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found some relevant information about Mosek's SDP solver capabilities:\n\nThe theoretical maximum for most kinds of objects in Mosek is 2^31, however you are likely to run out of RAM before that. This suggests that the practical limits are determined more by available memory than by hard-coded limits.\n\nRegarding benchmark information and problem size limits specifically for 2025, the search results don't contain a dedicated 2025 benchmark report with specific performance metrics or variable limits for Mosek's SDP solver. However, the results do provide some general context:\n\n- The emphasis in MOSEK is on solving large-scale sparse problems linear and conic optimization problems.\n\n- You cannot expect any current SDP solver to solve extremely large SDPs, as one usually becomes restricted by the available memory rather than by the solver speed.\n\n- All the optimizers available in MOSEK are built for the solution of large-scale sparse problems.\n\nFor more specific 2025 benchmark data on Mosek's SDP solver problem size limits and variable capacity, you may want to check the official Mosek documentation at docs.mosek.com or contact Mosek directly, as this information does not appear to be publicly available in standard web sources.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"94bdc7c4-76d6-42cb-a69c-363f9a2171d3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:05.511Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"995edb07-aede-4896-a7cf-93a326bb5b82","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"16be64a1-016b-4044-bd25-e0d6f1d00243","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a7db41848a47c8250","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KVZ7ATzGD2CGR1qXE12feU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Lasserre hierarchy polynomial optimization 2026 scalability large scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Full article: Revisiting the convergence rate of the Lasserre hierarchy for polynomial optimization over the hypercube\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/02331934.2026.2641624\"},{\"title\":\"[1709.04376] Lasserre hierarchy for large scale polynomial optimization in real and complex variables\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.04376\"},{\"title\":\"Lasserre Hierarchy for Large Scale Polynomial Optimization in Real and Complex Variables | SIAM Journal on Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/15M1034386\"},{\"title\":\"Lasserre hierarchy for large scale polynomial optimization ...\",\"url\":\"https://molzahn.github.io/pubs/josz_molzahn-large_scale_polynomial_optimization.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lasserre's Hierarchy in Polynomial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/lasserre-s-hierarchy\"},{\"title\":\"Multi-ordered Lasserre hierarchy for large scale polynomial optimization in real and complex variables | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/319700918_Multi-ordered_Lasserre_hierarchy_for_large_scale_polynomial_optimization_in_real_and_complex_variables\"},{\"title\":\"Lasserre Hierarchy for Polynomial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/lasserre-hierarchy-for-polynomial-optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Lasserre Hierarchy for Large Scale Polynomial Optimization in Real and Complex Variables - LAAS - Laboratoire d'Analyse et d'Architecture des Systèmes\",\"url\":\"https://laas.hal.science/hal-01592093\"},{\"title\":\"Lasserre Hierarchy for Large Scale Polynomial Optimization in Real and Complex Variables - Archive ouverte HAL\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-01592093\"},{\"title\":\"Global Optimization with Polynomials and the Problem of Moments | SIAM Journal on Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/S1052623400366802\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for \"Lasserre hierarchy polynomial optimization 2026 scalability large scale\". Here are the key findings:\n\n## Recent Developments in Lasserre Hierarchy for Large-Scale Optimization\n\nA 2026 paper revisits the convergence rate of the Lasserre hierarchy for polynomial optimization over the hypercube, published online in March 2026, examining how the sum-of-squares hierarchy provides a sequence of lower bounds.\n\n### Scalability Advances\n\nResearchers have proposed general notions to deal with large scale polynomial optimization problems, with efficiency demonstrated on optimal power flow problems, enabling the discovery of global minimizers on instances with up to 4,500 variables and 14,500 constraints.\n\n### Key Techniques for Large-Scale Problems\n\nThe Lasserre hierarchy has been generalized from real to complex numbers to enhance its tractability when dealing with complex polynomial optimization. A multi-ordered Lasserre hierarchy has been introduced to exploit sparsity in polynomial optimization problems while preserving global convergence.\n\n### Recent Performance Metrics\n\nIn large test cases, only a small fraction of constraints needed increased relaxation order, with first bounds computed in 320 seconds (real) versus 141 seconds (complex) for problems with approximately 4,584 variables, and global solutions in 900 seconds (real) versus 700 seconds (complex).\n\n### Broader Applications\n\nDeployment of these scalable, certified global methods extends to other domains involving nonconvex polynomial equations with structure: signal processing, control, large-scale combinatorial and graph-theoretic relaxations, and more.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2033e311-7e2c-4e77-82e1-35fcda940607","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:07.892Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"16be64a1-016b-4044-bd25-e0d6f1d00243","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3492440e-ed24-4460-bf12-872a09f22b5a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a7db41848a47c8250","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QULiYyuPod8PyWCfQTTLa3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Benders decomposition SDP master problem combinatorial optimization\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benders_decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"Benders’ decomposition of the unit commitment problem with semidefinite relaxation of AC power flow constraints - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S037877962030763X\"},{\"title\":\"Solving logic-based benders decomposition master problems with constraint programming and domain-independent dynamic programming | Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10601-025-09382-1\"},{\"title\":\"SDP-based Benders decomposition for solving p-median quadratic facility location problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305054825001479\"},{\"title\":\"Combining optimisation and simulation using logic-based Benders decomposition - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S037722172300591X\"},{\"title\":\"Perspectives on Using Benders Decomposition to Solve Two-Stage Stochastic Mixed-Integer Programs | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-57603-4_12\"},{\"title\":\"Improved Combinatorial Benders Decomposition for a Scheduling Problem with Unrelated Parallel Machines - Gomes - 2017 - Journal of Applied Mathematics - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1155/2017/9452762\"},{\"title\":\"language-reference/optimization-modeling-components/automatic-benders-decomposition/index.rst at master · aimms/language-reference\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/aimms/language-reference/blob/master/optimization-modeling-components/automatic-benders-decomposition/index.rst\"},{\"title\":\"Benders Decomposition - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/mathematics/benders-decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"The Benders Dual Decomposition Method | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.2019.1892\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for \"Benders decomposition SDP master problem combinatorial optimization.\" Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview of Benders Decomposition\n\nBenders decomposition is a technique in mathematical optimization that allows the solution of very large linear programming problems that have a special block structure. In Benders decomposition, the variables of the original problem are divided into two subsets so that a first-stage master problem is solved over the first set of variables, and the values for the second set of variables are determined in a second-stage subproblem for a given first-stage solution.\n\n## Master Problem and Algorithm\n\nInitially the set of cuts is empty. The set of cuts will be filled in a sequence of iterations by solving the inner maximization problem of the minimax formulation. The cuts both guide the master problem towards an optimal solution. Since Benders decomposition adds new constraints as it progresses towards a solution, the approach is called \"row generation\".\n\n## SDP Applications\n\nRecent research has explored combining Benders decomposition with semidefinite programming (SDP). One approach uses a QCQP formulation of the transmission constraints projected onto the space of semidefinite cones, for which the discrete unit commitment decisions are solved in a Benders' decomposition approach in order to overcome solutions with integrality gap due to a relaxation, while taking advantage of a series of convex SDP relaxations of the network. Additionally, semi-definite programming provides tight relaxations for the master problem, and new algorithms combining SDP and Benders decomposition outperform linearization and classical Benders decomposition.\n\n## Combinatorial Applications\n\nRecent work investigates using Constraint Programming and Domain-Independent Dynamic Programming to solve the master problem in Logic-based Benders Decomposition models, exploiting variable assignment bounds, variable assignment counting, and global constraints to construct combinatorial cut encodings.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b50bcabf-39af-4f33-a0b6-f1334d3e2530","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:08.030Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3492440e-ed24-4460-bf12-872a09f22b5a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"67fe3899-d12f-450f-9aac-18817a618fc4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a7db41848a47c8250","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVPkGX55UuQDm9YuBKHGDh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SDP relaxation rectangle packing 2D placement optimization survey\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1402.0557\"},{\"title\":\"Positions and covering: A two-stage methodology to obtain optimal solutions for the 2d-bin packing problem | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0229358\"},{\"title\":\"An efficient heuristic algorithm for two-dimensional rectangular packing problem with central rectangle\",\"url\":\"https://www.aimsciences.org/article/doi/10.3934/jimo.2018164\"},{\"title\":\"Survey for 2-D packing algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://www.csc.liv.ac.uk/~epa/surveyhtml.html\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement Approach\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/260039071_Optimal_Rectangle_Packing_An_Absolute_Placement_Approach\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal rectangle packing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220462008_Optimal_rectangle_packing\"},{\"title\":\"Robust Optimization for the Two-Dimensional Strip-Packing Problem with Variable-Sized Bins\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-7390/11/23/4781\"},{\"title\":\"Mitigating Dimensionality in 2D Rectangle Packing Problem under Reinforcement Learning Schema\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.09677v1\"},{\"title\":\"Two-dimensional packing problems: A survey | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/4870246_Two-dimensional_packing_problems_A_survey\"},{\"title\":\"[1402.0557] Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement Approach\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1402.0557\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for your query about SDP relaxation, rectangle packing, 2D placement optimization, and surveys. Here's a summary of the findings:\n\nThe search results reveal several important works and approaches in 2D rectangle packing and placement optimization:\n\n**Key Research Areas:**\n\nThe main research in two-dimensional orthogonal cutting and packing problems focuses on exact methods and relaxations for problems including finding a packing with minimum height, packing items into the minimum number of bins, finding a packing of maximum value, and determining the existence of a feasible packing.\n\n**Methodological Approaches:**\n\nA two-stage methodology called Positions and Covering (P&C) has been developed to solve the two-dimensional bin packing problem. Additionally, recent work employs the contiguous one-dimensional relaxation technique in conjunction with column generation, where a one-dimensional contiguous bin-packing problem (1D-CBPP) transforms the two-dimensional model into a one-dimensional variant through column generation to determine exact solutions and provide a tighter lower bound for the 2D problem.\n\n**Optimization Techniques:**\n\nSome methods use a relaxation similar to the cumulative constraint which requires that the sum of the heights of all rectangles overlapping a particular x-coordinate cannot exceed the height of the bounding box.\n\n**Foundational Surveys:**\n\nNumerous comprehensive surveys are available, including works by Lodi, Martello, & Vigo (2002); Lodi, Martello, & Monaci (2002); Dowsland & Dowsland (1992); and Sweeney & Paternoster (1992).\n\nThe search results contain various optimization approaches for rectangle packing but do not specifically highlight SDP (Semidefinite Programming) relaxation techniques in the top results. If you're specifically interested in SDP relaxation methods for this problem, you may want to search more specifically for semidefinite programming applications in packing problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"722b2d6c-31bc-484f-978e-6ac5592c97d2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:12.086Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"67fe3899-d12f-450f-9aac-18817a618fc4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
