{"parentUuid":"306d4a88-73db-4196-bd3b-d76a5a05001c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7db41848a47c8250","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HVngJ7W4vPBLVmPadn3Ngc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XCjZ5zRX9d3av6yQsbgcBC","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"quadratic assignment problem SDP relaxation bound facility layout 2024"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12234,"cache_read_input_tokens":22990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12234,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox4stafkUoMyiQW9Rzm","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"061d53b3-f265-493e-ae6e-1a7d99c042e3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:42.105Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3fd2ac68-92c4-45b5-856f-d713463198a5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a7db41848a47c8250","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KQjgLsUc9HgUoYZkxqevPa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"sum of squares\" SDP combinatorial optimization 2025 GPU solver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A user manual for cuHALLaR: A GPU accelerated low-rank semidefinite programming Solver – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2025/08/a-user-manual-for-cuhallar-a-gpu-accelerated-low-rank-semidefinite-programming-solver/\"},{\"title\":\"Sum-of-squares optimization — Grokipedia\",\"url\":\"https://grokipedia.com/page/Sum-of-squares_optimization\"},{\"title\":\"SDP Sum of Squares optimization - Optimization (Mathematical) - Julia Programming Language\",\"url\":\"https://discourse.julialang.org/t/sdp-sum-of-squares-optimization/88487\"},{\"title\":\"Improving Efficiency and Scalability of Sum of Squares Optimization: Recent Advances and Limitations – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2017/10/6256/\"},{\"title\":\"Semidefinite Programming | SIAM Review\",\"url\":\"https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/1038003\"},{\"title\":\"Sum-of-Squares Optimization Akilesh Tangella 1 Introduction\",\"url\":\"https://fisher.wharton.upenn.edu/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Thesis_Akilesh.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Google Summer of Code 2025 - Randomized SDP solver and improved preprocessing | Angelos Korakitis\",\"url\":\"https://angeloskorakitis.github.io/gsoc-2025\"},{\"title\":\"On solving the MAX-SAT using sum of squares – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2023/02/on-solving-the-max-sat-using-sum-of-squares/\"},{\"title\":\"SOS-SDP: an Exact Solver for Minimum Sum-of-Squares Clustering – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2021/04/8352/\"},{\"title\":\"Sum of Squares: OR Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.numberanalytics.com/blog/sum-of-squares-or-optimization-guide\"}]\n\nI found several relevant results about sum-of-squares (SOS) optimization, semidefinite programming (SDP), and GPU-accelerated solvers in the context of combinatorial optimization. Here are the key findings:\n\n## GPU-Accelerated SDP Solver\n\nA GPU-accelerated low-rank semidefinite programming solver (cuHALLaR) includes example problems such as SDP relaxations of the Matrix Completion and Maximum Stable Set problems, which are classic combinatorial optimization problems.\n\n## Recent Advances in SOS for Combinatorial Optimization (2025)\n\nGPU acceleration has been applied to monomial basis generation and matrix assembly in polynomial optimizations underlying SOS, parallelizing combinatorial enumeration and dense operations to speed up preprocessing by orders of magnitude on high-end hardware.\n\nAdditionally, recent advances as of 2025 have provided quantitative convergence rates for moment-SOS hierarchies, including frameworks for analyzing rates in infinite-dimensional linear programs and specific bounds for generalized moment problems with countable supports.\n\n## Convergence of SOS Hierarchies for Sparse Problems\n\nFor certain structured classes, such as polynomials with few monomials (sparse supports), tailored analyses show convergence at low hierarchy levels, often O(1) or linear in the sparsity pattern, leveraging chordal graph decompositions or correlative sparsity.\n\n## Applications and SDP Integration\n\nSparsity naturally arises in many real-world applications—such as control theory, combinatorial optimization, and signal processing, making sparse SDP solvers particularly valuable for these domains.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d591b301-dfa4-4e1d-b19d-8fae5cbec6b9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:47.981Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3fd2ac68-92c4-45b5-856f-d713463198a5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"306d4a88-73db-4196-bd3b-d76a5a05001c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a7db41848a47c8250","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KeivaZshyaNgrBbg7seJCv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cuLoRADS GPU SDP solver Burer-Monteiro low rank 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2407.15049] Accelerating Low-Rank Factorization-Based Semidefinite Programming Algorithms on GPU\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.15049\"},{\"title\":\"A user manual for cuHALLaR: A GPU accelerated low-rank semidefinite programming Solver – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2025/08/a-user-manual-for-cuhallar-a-gpu-accelerated-low-rank-semidefinite-programming-solver/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - COPT-Public/cuLoRADS: GPU-accelerated first-order low-rank SDP solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/COPT-Public/cuLoRADS\"},{\"title\":\"ICCOPT2025USC: Parallel Sessions 7F: GPU-Accelerated Ma...\",\"url\":\"https://iccopt2025usc.sched.com/event/1dqr7/parallel-sessions-7f-gpu-accelerated-mathematical-programming-part-ii\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerating Low-Rank Factorization-Based Semidefinite Programming Algorithms on GPU\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2407.15049v1\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerating Low-Rank Factorization-Based Semidefinite ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2407.15049\"},{\"title\":\"cuHALLaR: A GPU Accelerated Low-Rank Augmented Lagrangian\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Manuscript.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cuHALLaR: A GPU Accelerated Low-Rank Augmented Lagrangian Method for Large-Scale Semidefinite Programming Funding: Jacob M. Aguirre is supported by the National Science Foundation Graduate Research Fellowship under Grant No. DGE-2039655. Diego Cifuentes is supported by U.S. Office of Naval Research, N00014-23-1-2631. Renato D.C. Monteiro is supported by AFOSR Grant FA9550-25-1-0131.\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.13719\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerating Low-Rank Factorization-Based Semidefinite Programming Algorithms on GPU\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/papers/2407.15049\"},{\"title\":\"A nonlinear programming algorithm for solving semidefinite programs via low-rank factorization | Mathematical Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-002-0352-8\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about cuLoRADS and the related topics:\n\n## Overview\n\ncuLoRADS is an enhanced GPU-based first-order method solver written in Julia for low-rank semi-definite programming problems (SDPs).\n\n## Technical Background\n\nThe low-rank factorization-based SDP solver, LoRADS, involves both the classic Burer-Monteiro method and a novel splitting scheme with a starting logarithmic rank. The approach introduces an efficient method for calculating vital operators in low-rank factorization methods on GPUs and proposes a compression technique that exploits the column sparsity of the constraint matrix, reducing quadratic memory cost to the dependence on the number of nonzero elements.\n\n## Performance\n\nThe accelerated GPU version of LoRADS, cuLoRADS, can solve huge-scale semidefinite programming problems with remarkable efficiency by effectively leveraging GPU computational power. It can solve a set of MaxCut problems with 10^7 × 10^7 matrix variables in 10 seconds to 1 minute each on an NVIDIA H100 GPU.\n\n## Recent Developments (2025)\n\nA related GPU-accelerated solver has also been developed: cuHALLaR is a GPU accelerated low-rank semidefinite programming solver using Burer-Monteiro factorization, established as fast and numerically stable.\n\n## Availability\n\ncuLoRADS is free for academic use.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"75333607-8cb0-4fd4-b405-838828739b89","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:48.471Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"306d4a88-73db-4196-bd3b-d76a5a05001c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"061d53b3-f265-493e-ae6e-1a7d99c042e3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a7db41848a47c8250","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XCjZ5zRX9d3av6yQsbgcBC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"quadratic assignment problem SDP relaxation bound facility layout 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Novel SDP Relaxation for the Quadratic Assignment Problem using Cut Pseudo Bases\",\"url\":\"https://resources.mpi-inf.mpg.de/qap/\"},{\"title\":\"Quadratic Assignment Problem (QAP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/quadratic-assignment-problems-qap\"},{\"title\":\"[2408.05942] On the Exactness of SDP Relaxation for Quadratic Assignment Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.05942\"},{\"title\":\"A Novel SDP Relaxation for the Quadratic Assignment Problem Using Cut Pseudo Bases | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-45587-7_36\"},{\"title\":\"A Novel SDP Relaxation for the Quadratic Assignment Problem Using Cut Pseudo Bases | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/307940734_A_Novel_SDP_Relaxation_for_the_Quadratic_Assignment_Problem_Using_Cut_Pseudo_Bases\"},{\"title\":\"A new semide\\u001cnite programming relaxation for the quadratic assignment problem and its computational perspectives – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2013/08/3985/\"},{\"title\":\"On the Exactness of SDP Relaxation for Quadratic Assignment Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/papers/2408.05942\"},{\"title\":\"Computing Lower Bounds for the Quadratic Assignment Problem with an Interior Point Algorithm for Linear Programming | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.43.5.781\"},{\"title\":\"The Quadratic Assignment Problem | Management Science\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/mnsc.9.4.586\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - fsbravo/csdp: SDP relaxation techniques for the Quadratic Assignment Problem\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/fsbravo/csdp\"}]\n\nI've performed a web search for \"quadratic assignment problem SDP relaxation bound facility layout 2024\". Here are the key findings:\n\n## Recent 2024 Research\n\nThe Quadratic Assignment Problem (QAP) is a fundamental problem in combinatorial optimization with numerous applications in operation research, computer vision, and pattern recognition. A notable 2024 paper investigates the semidefinite relaxation (SDR) of the QAP and when the SDR recovers the global minimizer, showing that when noise is sufficiently smaller than signal in a signal-plus-noise model, the SDR is exact.\n\n## SDP Relaxation Approaches\n\nStandard semidefinite relaxations (SDP) lift the problem to a rank-one constraint on a positive semidefinite matrix embedding permutation structure. Recent work has also produced verifiable, deterministic, and purely algebraic sufficient conditions for SDP exactness—whenever these hold, the global optimum is attained at a permutation matrix and the relaxation is tight.\n\nFor scalability, blockwise and clique-based SDPs exploit problem structure to reformulate the global PSD constraint as a set of smaller PSD blocks, greatly improving scalability with strong empirical lower bounds in real-world applications.\n\n## Facility Layout Applications\n\nThe facility location problem is an example of QAP where n facilities are assigned to n sites at minimum cost, with flow between facilities contributing a cost equal to the product of the flow and the distance between assigned sites.\n\nThe search results show active research in improving SDP relaxation bounds for QAPs, with 2024 contributing theoretical advances in understanding when these relaxations are exact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"bce5a339-38b8-4354-8485-9f4ef513c429","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:49.399Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"061d53b3-f265-493e-ae6e-1a7d99c042e3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
